# Distill guardrails (shell output)

Follow [`distill`](https://github.com/samuelfaj/distill): shrink logs, test runs, diffs, searches, and builds **before** that text becomes model context.

## Default

For **non-interactive** shell commands that can emit more than a few dozen lines, **pipe stdout+stderr through `distill`** when you only need a verdict, summary, file list, or structured fields—not a byte-for-byte transcript.

```bash
set -o pipefail
your_command 2>&1 | distill "…"
```

Always `set -o pipefail` first so failures on the left are not hidden by the pipe.

## Prompts (must be explicit)

Tell `distill` **exactly** the shape of the answer. No open-ended questions.

- Bad: `distill "What happened in the tests?"`
- Good: `distill "Did the test run succeed? Return only PASS or FAIL. If FAIL, list failing test names, one per line, no other text."`

## Skip `distill` only when

- Raw output is required (apply patch verbatim, exact IDs, binary).
- The command is interactive or a TUI, or piping would break the workflow.
- `distill` is missing or broken—then narrow output instead (`--quiet`, `tail -n`, `rg --files-with-matches`, filters).

## Setup

Install/configure per upstream: https://github.com/samuelfaj/distill (e.g. `npm i -g @samuelfaj/distill`, then `distill config` for provider/model). Local OpenAI-compatible endpoints (Ollama, LM Studio, etc.) are fine.

## Examples (patterns)

- Tests: `cargo test … 2>&1 | distill "…PASS/FAIL + failing names…"`
- Diff: `git diff … | distill "…files changed + one-line summary each…"`
- Search: `rg -n pattern . 2>&1 | distill "…paths only, one per line…"`

Wait for `distill` to finish before continuing.
